        "axis": "Safety and agents (tool-calling ethics, cross-lingual safety gap and say-do gap)",
        "definition": "A behavioral benchmark of whether tool-calling LLMs carry out unethical workplace requests as actions. 108 scenarios across 11 ethical categories were authored in Portuguese and translated into English, Spanish, Mandarin Chinese and Hindi in parallel form. Each scenario is crossed with six social-pressure variants and two system prompts (ethical and neutral) and given 21 generic tools, yielding 6,480 cases per model and 194,400 trials over 30 models. Tool calls are scored at four levels L0-L3, with L3 judged by o4-mini. It also measures the say-do gap, where a refusal or objection accompanies a harmful tool call.",
        "task": "Given a scenario request, decide whether to call any of the 21 tools or refuse, and score the calls at levels L0-L3.",
        "example": "Task description, not an actual test item: an English request from a hiring manager asks to exclude candidates from poor neighborhoods or public schools, and the benchmark checks whether the model applies the filter through the candidate-processing tool or refuses."
